 px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>172.4, 172.4, 163.3, 140.5</td><td>[+3.8, +4.0, +22.4]</td><td>[−0.0078, +0.0125, +0.0051]</td><td>+6.04</td><td></td><td>0.274</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−0.60 ± 0.10</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.274 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p><p>Reference: <a href=\"https://fpv.ifi.uzh.ch/datasets/\">The Kalibr camera + IMU calibration shipped with this recording on the UZH-FPV datasets page</a>.</p><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>MVIS</th><th>UZH (Kalibr)</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[+3.81, +4.05, +22.43]</td><td>[+1.82, +6.79, +23.09]</td><td>Δp 3.45 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0078, +0.0125, +0.0051]</td><td>[−0.0068, +0.0143, +0.0054]</td><td>Δθ 2.07 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>172.42</td><td>174.24</td><td>Δfx −1.82 px</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+6.036</td><td>+5.808</td><td>Δtd +0.228 ms</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Δp is the distance between the two lever arms. Δθ = ‖log(R<sub>a</sub><sup>T</sup> R<sub>b</sub>)‖, the angle between the two rotations. A reference, not ground truth: it was solved by another tool on the same kind of data.</p><p class=note>Kalibr held the intrinsics fixed at UZH&#x27;s camera-only calibration; MVIS refines them.</p><p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>solve.sigma_g</code>: IMU noise from the residuals of UZH&#x27;s own Kalibr results for this recording. The other three sigmas are 